From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Kleinschmidt <kleinschmidtorama@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 10:32:26 -0400
Subject: [device] Make DeviceMonitorMessageWindow a NoDestructor

DeviceMonitorMessageWindow, which owns the DeviceMonitorWin instances,
was deleted by an AtExitManager callback. Any observer still alive at
that point is left holding a dangling pointer to its monitor.

This happens to SerialDeviceEnumeratorWin::UiThreadHelper at browser
shutdown. DeviceService lives in the UI thread's SequenceLocalStorage,
so it is destroyed by BrowserTaskExecutor::Shutdown(), which runs after
BrowserMainLoop has shut down the ThreadPool. DeviceService holds the
SerialPortManagerImpl in a SequenceBound on a ThreadPool sequence, so
the task that would delete it (and the enumerator and helper it owns) is
dropped. The helper's ScopedObservation is still live when AtExitManager
deletes the monitor, which fails CheckDanglingRawPtrBufferEmpty() at
exit when dangling pointer checks are enabled.

The AtExit registration dates from when DeviceMonitorMessageWindow owned
its own message window and needed to be destroyed in order with an
AtExit-managed HidService. Neither is true anymore: it listens on
gfx::SingletonHwnd, which is itself a NoDestructor, and HidService is
owned by DeviceService. Make it a base::NoDestructor so the monitors
outlive all of their observers.

Bug: 572741653
Change-Id: I85aa5586edab522b6fde5c77a5e4515b848a886b

Upstreamed at https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8561777.
This patch can be removed once that CL lands.

